{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019bVNXM6ppPNF69cws4KDVm","type":"tool_result","content":"2543\t=== APPEND C:\\dev\\lodestar\\certcomp\\..\\Book-KCNA/knowledge-base/concepts/control-loop.md ===\n2544\t\n2545\t## Chapter 15 update (2026-08-31) — ⚑⚑ THE BOOK'S PRIMARY ZENITH LANDS HERE\n2546\t\n2547\tChapter 15 §7 performs the loop's final and largest substitution: **desired state moves out of\n2548\tetcd and into a Git repository, and nothing else about the architecture changes.**\n2549\t\n2550\tArgo CD's application controller \"is a Kubernetes controller which continuously monitors running\n2551\tapplications and compares the current, live state against the desired target state (as specified\n2552\tin the repo).\" [source: argocd-architecture-2026-08-31] Three claims: it is the thing Ch 3 §6\n2553\tdefined; it does the thing Ch 3 §6 said controllers do; **only the location of the desired state\n2554\tis new.**\n2555\t\n2556\t⚠ **NO ORDINAL — the instruction on this shard from ch-09's Stage 14 stands, and Ch 15 is the\n2557\treason it exists.** term-ownership.md:754 sanctions exactly two control-loop counts in the whole\n2558\tbook: Ch 6's two-altitudes framing, and Ch 15 §7's \"third time.\" Chapter 15 spends the reserved\n2559\tthird correctly and adds nothing. **Ch 17 §4 collects the thread and must not add to the count.**\n2560\t\n2561\t⚑ **SHIP-BLOCKER inherited:** the §7 figure must visually rhyme with `ch03-fig02`, and as drawn\n2562\tit does not. See [[control-loop-pointed-at-a-repository]].\n2563\t\n2564\t=== END APPEND ===\n2565\t\n2566\t=== APPEND C:\\dev\\lodestar\\certcomp\\..\\Book-KCNA/knowledge-base/concepts/status.md ===\n2567\t\n2568\t## Chapter 15 update (2026-08-31) — the strongest single extension of this shard"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6f0b7fa2-24e7-485f-9ba0-7e639d285e38","uuid":"c72e9661-0847-41a6-9fd0-4b62ca31a82f","timestamp":"2026-08-31T15:00:48.781Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\.pipeline-state\\ch-15\\kb-manifest.md","content":"=== APPEND C:\\dev\\lodestar\\certcomp\\..\\Book-KCNA/knowledge-base/concepts/control-loop.md ===\n\n## Chapter 15 update (2026-08-31) — ⚑⚑ THE BOOK'S PRIMARY ZENITH LANDS HERE\n\nChapter 15 §7 performs the loop's final and largest substitution: **desired state moves out of\netcd and into a Git repository, and nothing else about the architecture changes.**\n\nArgo CD's application controller \"is a Kubernetes controller which continuously monitors running\napplications and compares the current, live state against the desired target state (as specified\nin the repo).\" [source: argocd-architecture-2026-08-31] Three claims: it is the thing Ch 3 §6\ndefined; it does the thing Ch 3 §6 said controllers do; **only the location of the desired state\nis new.**\n\n⚠ **NO ORDINAL — the instruction on this shard from ch-09's Stage 14 stands, and Ch 15 is the\nreason it exists.** term-ownership.md:754 sanctions exactly two control-loop counts in the whole\nbook: Ch 6's two-altitudes framing, and Ch 15 §7's \"third time.\" Chapter 15 spends the reserved\nthird correctly and adds nothing. **Ch 17 §4 collects the thread and must not add to the count.**\n\n⚑ **SHIP-BLOCKER inherited:** the §7 figure must visually rhyme with `ch03-fig02`, and as drawn\nit does not. See [[control-loop-pointed-at-a-repository]].\n\n=== END APPEND ===\n\n=== APPEND C:\\dev\\lodestar\\certcomp\\..\\Book-KCNA/knowledge-base/concepts/status.md ===\n\n## Chapter 15 update (2026-08-31) — the strongest single extension of this shard","numLines":26,"startLine":2543,"totalLines":3270}}}
